Moon data (frontend/public/moon/, generated with tools/moon/build_moon.py), public domain:
- LROC color and global LOLA relief: NASA Scientific Visualization Studio, "CGI Moon Kit"
  (https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4720).
- Polar LOLA relief (LDEM_80S_80MPP_ADJ): NASA Planetary Geodesy Data Archive
  (https://pgda.gsfc.nasa.gov/products/90), Barker et al.
- Crater coordinates: USGS/IAU Gazetteer of Planetary Nomenclature.
- "moon_03" regolith texture for the rover ground: Poly Haven (https://polyhaven.com), CC0.

Mars data (frontend/public/mars/, generated with tools/mars/build_mars.py), public domain:
- Color: colorized Viking MDIM2.1 global mosaic (USGS Astrogeology), served by NASA Mars Trek
  (https://trek.nasa.gov/mars).
- Relief: "HRSC and MOLA Blended Digital Elevation Model at 200m v2", Fergason, Hare and Laura (2018),
  USGS Astrogeology (https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/mars_mgs_mola_mex_hrsc_blended_dem_global_200m).
- Site coordinates: USGS/IAU Gazetteer of Planetary Nomenclature.
- Rock and outcrop texture on Mars: "rock_face_03" from Poly Haven (https://polyhaven.com), CC0.
- Rover ground texture on Mars: "Textura uniforme de suelo marciano rojizo", chosen by the team (color only;
  normal and AO derived in tools/mars/build_mars.py; not scanned data).

3D models (frontend/public/models/):
- curiosity_rover.glb, skycrane.glb, aeroshell.glb (Curiosity / MSL entry, descent and landing),
  msl.glb (MSL cruise stage) and atlas_v_541.glb (Atlas V 541 launcher) are based on NASA's public
  3D models (NASA 3D Resources: https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/,
  https://github.com/nasa/NASA-3D-Resources). The team modified them so they run in a browser game:
  fewer polygons, parts split and named so they can be articulated (suspension, arm, drill, sky crane,
  heat shield), and textures resized and compressed. The export steps are in tools/msl/README.md.
  Use of these models does not imply endorsement by NASA, and no NASA logos or marks are used.
- The orbiter and the hangar spacecraft are not model files: they are built in code from the game's
  parts (frontend/src/mission-architect/three/spacecraft.ts).

Sky, Earth and trajectories:
- Star sky: Tycho-2 star map skybox bundled with CesiumJS (Apache 2.0).
- Earth: Natural Earth II imagery bundled with CesiumJS, public domain.
- Moon transfer trajectory (frontend/public/trajectories/moon_transfer.json): computed with GMAT.
